# -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Steam Reception Predictor — .gitignore
# -------------------------------------------------------------------

# ── Generated model artefacts ───────────────────────────────────────
# These files are produced by running `python train_models.py` and are
# intentionally NOT committed for the following reasons:
#
#   1. Size: *.joblib files total ~10 MB; steam_clean.csv is ~13 MB.
#      Git is a poor store for large binaries — they bloat clone size
#      permanently even after deletion.
#
#   2. Reproducibility: committing binaries makes it easy to forget to
#      retrain after changing feature engineering. The rule "models/
#      is always the output of the current code on the current data"
#      is enforced by keeping it out of version control.
#
#   3. Data lineage: steam_clean.csv is a derivative of data/steam.csv.
#      Committing the derivative without the source is misleading.
#
# If you need to share trained models across machines or with a team,
# use a proper model registry (MLflow, DVC, or a shared S3 bucket)
# rather than committing them to git.
# -------------------------------------------------------------------
models/*.joblib
models/meta.json
models/steam_clean.csv

# Raw dataset (large binary, distribute separately)
data/steam.csv

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Streamlit local cache
.streamlit/

# IDE / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
*.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Scratch / diagnostic scripts (not part of the product)
diagnose.py
